// Idrenne's Fire (Fire_2; bible 4.5, 8.5 [F 9.2]): the game saying the true ending's requirement aloud, plainly,
// including the clans' rot (3.6: they were refused anchoring; the philosophy came after). Then the region's decision
// (whether to survey the Steppe at all) and the keystone, given up laughing. No cost. Deliberately.
// Lifting it wakes the Fallen Star in the crater below (6.10): the one cost.

title: Fire_Idrenne
---
<<if has_flag("windreach.fire.witnessed")>>
    Idrenne: Warm your hands. It's only a fire now. It was only a fire before, too. #still #line:00249e3
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("windreach.camp.walked")>>
    Idrenne: Walk the three fires first. I'll say it once, to someone who's walked them. #still #line:0e2fffd
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: You had a question. Isolde had the same one. Ask it. #line:058964b
-> How do you hold a place? #line:0265fd2
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> How do I stop it fading? #line:0bd809b
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> Do places need holding at all? #line:02e71c6
    <<voice drift windreach>>
Idrenne: I learned it here, at this fire, the year the Guild said no to us. #line:07f4168
Idrenne: We asked to be anchored. We were poor. They said the Steppe wasn't worth a stone. #line:0c1f7e9
Idrenne: So we made a philosophy of it afterwards. I'll not pretend otherwise. It works anyway. #plant:9.2 #line:0ffb455
Idrenne: A place holds when it's lived in. Walked. Every name in it said out loud. #line:0604ff6
Idrenne: One town can't do it alone. It takes everyone you've met, singing the same walk. #plant:9.2 #line:080a49a
Idrenne: And the stones go back where they came from. You don't keep a place in a vault. #line:0c1e91b
<<flag windreach.fire.witnessed 1>>
<<if has_flag("windreach.hale.finished")>>
    Idrenne: Your lens bird finished his sighting. The Steppe's on Guild paper now. We'll keep walking it. #line:087acb7
<<else>>
    Idrenne: Now. You carry a quill. Will you draw the Steppe? #line:0c3ecaf
    -> I'll draw it. For you, not them. #line:067d032
        Idrenne: Paper goes where paper goes. I learned that at your Plateau's gate. Draw well. #line:08daa5a
        <<flag windreach.survey.decided 1>>
        <<voice surveyor windreach>>
    -> I'll leave it undrawn. #line:0095eb0
        Idrenne: Then it's ours, and the grass's. Thank you. #line:0461d44
        <<flag windreach.survey.decided 2>>
        <<voice warden windreach>>
    -> I'll walk it instead. Every year. <<if walk_known()>> #line:0978c7e
        Idrenne: Ha. Then you're one of us, and it's held the old way. Come back hungry. #line:007dd0f
        <<flag windreach.survey.decided 3>>
        <<voice drift windreach>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: Oh. And this. Our cooking-stone. Your Guild would call it a keystone. #line:0685f52
Idrenne: Take it. We'll cook on a flat rock. No cost. I mean it. Ha! #line:0077ebb
<<flag keystone.windreach 1>>
<<flag windreach.star.woken 1>>
Fire: Below the rise, in the crater, iron groans. Forty years an anvil. It sits up. #line:0587b9d
===

title: Star_Idrenne
---
<<if not has_flag("windreach.star.woken")>>
    Idrenne: The smiths' anvil. Iron from the sky. Asleep since I was a girl. Mind your feet anyway. #still #line:0982b82
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("boss.fallen_star.defeated")>>
    <<if not has_flag("windreach.star.cold")>>
        Idrenne: Ha. Told you. No cost. Well. One. #line:00d8c4f
        Idrenne: The anvil's cold. The smiths will complain for a year. They like complaining. #line:0d7679e
        <<flag windreach.star.cold 1>>
    <<else>>
        Idrenne: Cold iron. The smiths found something new to complain about. Good for them. #still #line:0fcfb87
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: There it is. The cost. Mind the iron. #still #line:07bf6d8
-> I'll put it back to sleep. #line:0883db4
    Idrenne: Swing hard. It's been hit for forty years. It'll want to hit back. #still #line:0a64cef
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> What does it want? #line:0092314
    Idrenne: A swing. Forty years our anvil. It's owed one. #still #line:0d0cab1
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> Leave it. It's earned the rest. #line:0c446af
    Idrenne: Then it stands there awake till it's tired. We'll smith somewhere else. #still #line:0b793b8
    <<voice drift windreach>>
<<flag windreach.star.met 1>>
===
